  "description": "BUCLUH crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C8 H20 N1 O2 1+,C100 H200 Mn5 N8 O64 Pr8 1-,5(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Pr1 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr2 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr3 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr4 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr5 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr6 (Pr) has 9 O neighbors; Pr7 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Pr8 (Pr) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.476-4.261 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.72-118.01°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C118H235Mn5N14O66Pr8. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
